QtZpl Font A Native
==================

resources/fonts/font_a_native.ttf is a renamed derivative of the licensed
DejaVu Sans Mono source already embedded as resources/fonts/font_a.ttf.
Original source SHA-256:
b4a6c3e4faab8773f4ff761d56451646409f29abedd68f05d38c2df667d3c582

Copyright (c) 2003 by Bitstream, Inc. All Rights Reserved.
DejaVu changes are in public domain. The complete font license is in LICENSE
and remains embedded in the derivative's name table.
Upstream: https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/
License: https://dejavu-fonts.github.io/License.html

QtZpl modifications: affine normalization of glyph outlines to printer Font A
metrics, a 1365-unit fixed advance, rounded design-grid coordinates, regenerated
TrueType hints, and the new family name "QtZpl Font A Native". The transformation
coefficients in src/printer_font_metrics.hpp were checked against Labelary
vector output; no downloaded Labelary font subset is a generation input.

Reproduction
------------
Run tools/generate_font_a.py with FontForge 20251009, source commit
c41bdb922285f35defd1e1385adfd13bde1ab32a, and ttfautohint 1.8.4:

  fontforge -lang=py -script tools/generate_font_a.py --ttfautohint PATH

FontForge: https://fontforge.org/
ttfautohint: https://freetype.org/ttfautohint/
ttfautohint options: -x 0 (disable the screen-font x-height increase).
ttfautohint's COPYING grants an explicit exception for copying, distributing,
and modifying generated font bytecode independently of its tool licenses:
https://github.com/fonttools/ttfautohint-mirror/blob/master/COPYING
The generator uses only the committed original font and metric coefficients;
it normalizes output timestamps and SFNT checksums for reproducible assets.
These tools are generation-time tools, not build or runtime requirements.

Rendering uses Qt's bundled FreeType (or the configured system FreeType) with
native TrueType hints and a monochrome raster. Hints are fitted at the selected
height before horizontal stretching. Each render owns its font face and cache.
